 `src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+
+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` and answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }`
+  (tickets newly imported, dishes sold on them). A ticket already imported is
+  skipped. If a row is invalid (`bad_request`) or an item runs out
+  (`import_out_of_stock`, 409), nothing is imported and the message names the
+  row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers, per item,
+  `{ itemId, name, theoretical, actual, difference }`: use from sales sold in
+  those days, every `consume` movement in those days, and actual minus
+  theoretical. Only items where either is above zero are listed.
